msgstr "Instalação do Sshfs"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:93
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Sshfs</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale <application>Sshfs</application> executando os seguintes comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:97
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr --buildtype=release .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr --buildtype=release .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:104
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr "Esse pacote não vem com uma suíte de teste."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:108
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:111
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:115
#, xml-text
msgid "Using Sshfs"
msgstr "Usando o Sshfs"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:118
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To mount an ssh server you need to be able to log into the server. For "
"example, to mount your remote home folder to the local ~/examplepath (the "
"directory must exist and you must have permissions to write to it):"
msgstr ""
"Para montar um servidor SSH, você precisa estar apto(a) a se logar no "
"servidor. Por exemplo, para montar sua pasta \"home\" remota no "
"~/caminho_de_exemplo local (o diretório precisa existir e você precisa ter "
"permissões para gravar nele):"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:123
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>sshfs example.com:/home/userid ~/examplepath</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sshfs exemplo.com:/home/userid ~/caminho_de_exemplo</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:126
#, xml-text
msgid "When you've finished work and want to unmount it again:"
msgstr "Quando tiver terminado o trabalho e quiser desmontá-lo novamente:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:129
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>fusermount3 -u ~/example</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>fusermount3 -u ~/exemplo</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:132
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You can also mount an <application>sshfs</application> filesystem at boot by"
" adding an entry similar to the following in the "
"<filename>/etc/fstab</filename> file:"
msgstr ""
"Você também consegue montar um sistema de arquivos "
"<application>sshfs</application> na inicialização adicionando uma entrada "
"semelhante à seguinte no arquivo <filename>/etc/fstab</filename>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:137
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>userid@example.com:/path /media/path fuse.sshfs "
"_netdev,IdentityFile=/home/userid/.ssh/id_rsa 0 0</literal>"
msgstr ""
"<literal>id_de_usuario@exemplo.com:/caminho /media/caminho fuse.sshfs "
"_netdev,IdentityFile=/home/id_de_usuario/.ssh/id_rsa 0 0</literal>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/filesystems/sshfs.xml:140
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"See <command>man 1 sshfs</command> and <command>man 8 mount.fuse3</command> "
"for all available mount options."
msgstr ""
"Veja-se <command>man 1 sshfs</command> e <command>man 8 "
"mount.fuse3</command> para todas as opções disponíveis de montagem."

